From fa510fae5e886a12b62a92acb48c136b0ae04b95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:57:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(2d): peck a contour dive deeper than one stepdown
 below the cut floor

A tabbed level of a 2D Contour entered each later tab window (and, with
the stay-down ramp preset, window 0 too) by one plunge from the retract
plane to the level. The levels above cut that lead-in start only at the
ring start, so the plunge went up to 18 mm into uncut stock.

The new contour_peck module reads the floor that the posted cuts (feeds
at one height and straight plunge columns) left under the full tool
disc. Below a ring's first level, the wall-side graze dive and the dive
past a tab peck one stepdown at a time where they would go deeper than
one stepdown below that floor. One note says it.

contour_tab_entry.rs counts plunge columns in its floor oracle, asserts
every descent of the four presets, and pins the new window readings.

Fixes #3678

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
